{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Match/SimpH.html#Lean.Meta.Match.simpH?\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Match</span>.<span class=\"name\">simpH?</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">h</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">numEqs</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns the simplified form of the overlap hypothesis `h` of an equation for a `match`\nalternative, or `none` if `h` is redundant. `h` must be of the form `∀ xs, eqs → False`, where\n`eqs` are `numEqs` equations. See `simpH` for the simplification steps and examples.\n\nOnly the statement is computed: `h` is the type of the hypothesis as generated from the patterns,\nand the result is the type used in the statement of the equation.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Match/SimpH.html#Lean.Meta.Match.simpH?","kind":"def","line":198,"name":"Lean.Meta.Match.simpH?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Match/SimpH.lean#L198-L211"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Match/SimpH.html#Lean.Meta.Match.simpH\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Match</span>.<span class=\"name\">simpH</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">mvarId</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.MVarId\">MVarId</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">numEqs</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.MVarId\">MVarId</a>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Simplifies an overlap hypothesis of an equation for a `match` alternative.\n\nThe equation for an alternative has one hypothesis for each previous alternative that overlaps\nit. The hypothesis states that the previous alternative does not match. Before it is simplified,\nit has the form `∀ xs, eqs → False`, where `xs` are the pattern variables of the previous\nalternative, and `eqs` are `numEqs` equations `p = q` or `p ≍ q` between the patterns of the two\nalternatives.\n\nThe type of the goal `mvarId` must be a hypothesis of this form. This function returns\n- `none` if the hypothesis is redundant: the equations `eqs` are contradictory, and `mvarId` has\n  been closed. Example: `none = some 0 → False`.\n- `some mvarId'` otherwise. The type of `mvarId'` is the simplified hypothesis, and `mvarId` has\n  been proved using `mvarId'`.\n\nThe equations are processed one at a time.\n- `p = q` is removed if `p` and `q` are definitionally equal.\n- `p = x`, where `x` is one of the variables `xs`, is removed, and `x` is replaced with `p`.\n- `p ≍ q` is replaced with `p = q` if `p` and `q` have the same type.\n- An equation between constructor applications is replaced with the equations between their\n  fields. If the constructors are different, the hypothesis is redundant.\n- Any other equation is kept.\n\nThe simplified hypothesis is `∀ xs', eqs' → False`, where `eqs'` are the equations that were kept,\nand `xs'` are the variables in `xs` that occur in them.\n\nExamples, where `n : Nat` and `x : Nat × Nat` are variables of the alternative being processed:\n- `some n = some 0 → False` is simplified to `n = 0 → False`.\n- `∀ m, some n = some (m + 1) → False` is simplified to `∀ m, n = m + 1 → False`.\n- `∀ a, n = a → x = (a, 0) → False` is simplified to `x = (n, 0) → False`.\n- `∀ m, some n = some m → False` is simplified to `False`: the previous alternative always matches.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Match/SimpH.html#Lean.Meta.Match.simpH","kind":"def","line":127,"name":"Lean.Meta.Match.simpH","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Match/SimpH.lean#L127-L196"}}],"imports":["Lean.Meta.Basic","Lean.Meta.Tactic.Cleanup","Lean.Meta.Tactic.Contradiction"],"instances":[],"name":"Lean.Meta.Match.SimpH"}